    "inscriptions": [
      {
        "inscription": "海雲初破月團團，獨鶴高飛夜未殘。\n一片笙簫湖水上，玉妃含笑倚闌干。\n\n王元章作",
        "inscription_translation": "Artist's inscription, signature, and 2 seals:\n\nA break in the sea of clouds unveils the circle of moon. \nA single crane flies high as the night is still young. \nThe limpid sounds of pan-pipe and flute sweep over the lake. \nThe jade concubine smiles faintly and leans over the railing.\n\nMade by Wang Yuanzhang",
        "inscription_remark": null,
        "sortorder": 1
      },
      {
        "inscription": "8 additional seals: 6 of the Qianlong 乾隆 emperor (r. 1736–95); 2 of Dong Gao 董誥 (1740–1818).",
        "inscription_translation": null,
        "inscription_remark": null,
        "sortorder": 2
      }
